\section{Standard errors, degrees of freedom and intervals}{

The coefficients and thresholds are tested by Wald z. Cluster-robust
variance is \code{"CR1"}, from \code{\link[sandwich:vcovCL]{sandwich::vcovCL()}}: the CR0 sandwich scaled
by \eqn{G/(G-1)}{G/(G-1)}, \code{G} the number of clusters, the one cluster
estimator of these classes; \code{"CR0"}, \code{"CR2"} and \code{"CR3"} are refused
rather than mapped. The thresholds take their uncertainty from the same
clustered matrix. A \code{clm} fit with a scale or nominal component has no
estimating functions in \code{ordinal} for those parts, so no sandwich can be
built for it.

Hierarchical comparison (\code{nested = TRUE}). Nested \code{polr} or \code{clm} fits
are compared by likelihood-ratio test, \code{c("lrt_change", "p_change")};
under \code{"CR1"} the change test is the Wald chi-square of the added
coefficients on the robust matrix. See \emph{Hierarchical (nested) model
comparison} in \code{\link[=table_regression]{table_regression()}}.
}

\section{Fit statistics}{

\code{polr}, \code{clm} and an ordinal \code{rms::lrm} default to
\code{c("nobs", "pseudo_r2_mcfadden", "aic")}. \code{"nobs"} and the BIC
follow the engine's
\code{\link[stats:nobs]{stats::nobs()}}, which for a weighted \code{polr} or \code{clm} fit is the sum of
the weights. The deviance R-squared is refused for ordinal models, where
it equals McFadden's. Cumulative-link mixed models show the fit
statistics of the mixed models (n, groups, AIC, BIC), without an
R-squared; see \link{table_regression_mixed}.
}

\section{Cumulative-link mixed models}{

\code{ordinal::clmm()} fits, and \code{glmmTMB::glmmTMB()} fits with
\code{family = glmmTMB::ordinal()}, keep the \code{Thresholds} block and add the
\verb{Random effects} block described in \link{table_regression_mixed}. Their
inference is Wald only: the AME columns, a robust \code{vcov},
\code{ci_method = "profile"} and \code{standardized} are refused, as is
\code{nested = TRUE} for \code{clmm}. The random-effects likelihood-ratio test of
the note refits its null model with the link actually fitted.
}

\section{What is refused, and why}{

\itemize{
\item \verb{HC*}, \code{"bootstrap"}, \code{"jackknife"}, and the \verb{CR*} tokens
other than \code{"CR1"}: \code{"CR1"} is the one robust estimator of these
classes.
\item A robust \code{vcov} for a \code{clm} fit with a scale or nominal
component, and for the cumulative-link mixed models.
\item \code{exponentiate = TRUE} under a link whose exponential is not a
ratio, and in the cloglog cases above.
\item \code{standardized}, for every class of this family.
\item For the cumulative-link mixed models, the AME,
\code{ci_method = "profile"}, and \code{nested = TRUE} for \code{clmm}.
}
}

